// from the provisioner's OWN configuration -- and a `name` matched by
// ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,62}$, and it lives at <parent root>/<name>. Everything
// the provisioner creates carries an ownership mark, checked before it resizes,
// snapshots or deletes anything: it never touches what it did not create.
//
// Create and Delete are idempotent by name, as CSI's are: the same name with
// the same parameters is OK and answers with the volume that exists; the same
// name with different parameters is ALREADY_EXISTS; deleting what is not there
// is OK.
//
